# Append-only JSONL stores — merged by git's built-in `union` driver.
#
# Both files below are append-only by construction: every row is written by one writer
# (`tools/ledger.py append`, `tools/insights.py`) under a lock, so two lanes appending
# concurrently can never have EDITED the same line — they can only have added different
# lines at the same end. That is precisely the shape `union` merges: it takes lines from
# BOTH sides instead of emitting conflict markers, so a concurrent-append conflict resolves
# to both rows, never to a file carrying `<<<<<<<` inside a JSON stream.
#
# The driver removes the CONFLICT, not the RACE. A row's `n` is assigned at append, so two
# branches that both took the same `n` still owe a re-mint of one of them
# (`docs/instruments/ledger.md` §9.1) — a union merge will happily keep both rows, and two
# rows sharing an `n` is a defect the merge cannot see.
#
# `union` is built in: no `merge.union.driver` config is needed, and setting one to `true`
# would REPLACE the 3-way union with a no-op that keeps whichever side git happened to
# check out. The attribute alone is the whole mechanism.
evidence/ledger.jsonl merge=union
evidence/insights.jsonl merge=union
